From: iimmyy <i.a.martins001@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:31:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] ggml-hexagon: Q3_K on the v68 NPU in the same 32-row
 tiles (low 2 bits in the Q2_K layout, high-bit planes, packed 6-bit scales
 unpacked on the DSP, exact integer math as ggml_vec_dot_q3_K_q8_K); co-op
 copy and q8_K pre-quantization shared with Q2_K. NPU vs board CPU KL 0.004 on
 E4B Q3_K. Open: matrices over 131072 rows (the full dictionary) come out
 wrong, kept off the NPU. test-backend-ops: tile-shaped Q2_K/Q3_K/Q4_0 cases

